utdown, extreme performance throttling, or permanent damage.//// Signed value; in Celsius.//// Indicates the maximum temperature in degrees Celsius at which the device is capable of// operating continuously without degrading operation or reliability.//// Signed value; in Celsius.// Some devices may report more than one temperature information as there can be multiple sensors implemented.//// Input parameters for IOCTL_STORAGE_SET_TEMPERATURE_THRESHOLD////// Indicate the target of the request other than the device handle/object itself.// This is used in "Flags" field of data structures.//// Signed value; in Celsius.// If TRUE, set the OverThreshold value; Otherwise, set the UnderThreshold value.//// Parameters for StorageAdapterPhysicalTopologyProperty (or StorageDevicePhysicalTopologyProperty) & PropertyStandardQuery////// Input parameters for StorageAdapterPhysicalTopologyProperty (or StorageDevicePhysicalTopologyProperty) & PropertyStandardQuery// uses data structure STORAGE_PROPERTY_QUERY.////// Out parameters for StorageAdapterPhysicalTopologyProperty (or StorageDevicePhysicalTopologyProperty) & PropertyStandardQuery// uses data structure STORAGE_PHYSICAL_TOPOLOGY_DESCRIPTOR////// Multiple roles are allowed for a single device.//// 3.5 inch nominal form factor// 2.5 inch nominal form factor// 1.8 inch nominal form factor// Less than 1.8 inch nominal form factor// Embedded on board.// Memory card such as SD, CF.// mSATA// M.2// PCIe card plug into slot.// DIMM Slot// Value(s) of bitmask from STORAGE_COMPONENT_ROLE_xxx// Supported storage spec version. For example: SBC 3, SATA 3.2, NVMe 1.2// in unit of Kilo-Bytes (1024 bytes).// Reserved for future.// Supported storage spec version. For example: AHCI 1.3.1// Reserve for future.// 0 or 1// Offset from beginning of this data structure. The buffer contains an array of STORAGE_PHYSICAL_ADAPTER_DATA.// >= 1// Offset from beginning of this data structure. The buffer contains an array of STORAGE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_DATA.// 