ed Unicode string of the adapter's serial number.////// Output buffer for StorageDeviceZonedDeviceProperty & PropertyStandardQuery//// Count of zones in this group.// In Bytes//// Size of this structure serves as the version////// Size of buffer. The returned value indicates how big the buffer should be// to store complete data.////// Zoned device type////// Total zone count////// Zone Attributes//// Host managed device only// Host aware device only//// Zone Layout Information, to provide a picture about locations of different type of zones on disk.// The zone layout starts from the first zone, and groups together zones with same type and size.////// Output buffer for StorageDeviceLocationProperty & PropertyStandardQuery////// Output buffer for StorageDeviceNumaProperty.//// If the query for this property is successful, then the caller should// validate the NumaNode field before using it to optimize any operations.// That is, the caller should ensure the NumaNode value is less than or equal// to the system's highest NUMA node value and the NumaNode value is not equal// to STORAGE_DEVICE_NUMA_NODE_UNKNOWN.////// Output buffer for StorageDeviceUnsafeShutdownCount.//// On persistent memory devices, the unsafe shutdown count is the number of times// the logical persistent memory disk was shut down in a way that might have caused// data loss.////// Parameters for StorageDeviceEnduranceProperty & PropertyStandardQuery////// Input parameters for StorageDeviceEnduranceProperty & PropertyStandardQuery// uses data structure STORAGE_PROPERTY_QUERY.////// Out parameters for StorageDeviceEnduranceProperty  & PropertyStandardQuery// For endurance info fields, ValidFields represents bit mapping of valid fields.//// ValidFields represents bit mapping of valid fields of any type// Eg: Bit 0 stands for GroupId, Bit 1 stands for Flags, Bit 3 for BytesReadCount// Set Id Eg: Set Id for NVMe sets// TRUE if information is shared with multiple units/groups// Used life percentage// Total by